On-chip rate microbenchmarks (GPU 0, serial under flock; bench/micro_r5.py lds | mfma, bench/dma_bw.py).
lds: ds_read rate per CU vs resident waves, lin = linear, s1a = the stage-1 A read pattern, dma = DMA loads
  in flight per wave. mfma: fp4 16x16x128 with e8m0 scales, interleaved ds_reads per MFMA.
dma: buffer_load -> LDS rate, contiguous / gathered 16 x 64 B rows / gathered 8 x 128 B rows.
Used by bench/roofline.py on-chip floor: LDS 280 B/ns/CU, MFMA 9.2 PF, TA 27.05 / 17.44 TB/s.

